<SeoArticle title="ARM Framework: Five Primitives for Accountable AI Agents | Coreweaver Labs" description="The ARM Framework defines five practical primitives for accountable AI agents: authority, signal architecture, recovery, escalation, and immutable audit history." canonical={canonical} eyebrow="Accountable agents · framework" heading="ARM Framework." lede="Five primitives for agents that can operate within authority, recover safely, escalate clearly, and leave an auditable record." section="AI Mastery">
  <p>The ARM Framework is Coreweaver Labs’ operating pattern for accountable agentic systems. It does not assume one model, vendor, tool protocol, or orchestration library. The primitives describe the control surfaces that any implementation should make explicit.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Primitive</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mandate Chain</td><td>Connect each material action to a named objective, owner, and scope.</td></tr><tr><td>Signal Architecture</td><td>Make sources, conflicts, confidence, and decision inputs explicit.</td></tr><tr><td>Checkpoint Recovery</td><td>Persist durable state so a workflow can resume instead of silently restarting.</td></tr><tr><td>Graceful Escalation</td><td>Define triggers and named humans for uncertainty or policy boundaries.</td></tr><tr><td>Immutable Audit Sovereignty</td><td>Preserve a tamper-evident history of material actions and decisions.</td></tr></tbody></table>
  <p>ARM connects to the <a href="/ai-mastery/trust-infrastructure/">Trust Infrastructure</a> layer, while the public-web expression of its evidence discipline appears in <a href="/geo/signal-architecture/">Signal Architecture</a> and the <a href="/geo-compass/anti-slop/">Anti-Slop Standard</a>.</p>
